 "notes": "Old models kept as versions where they fit an archetype; Hawkstone, Galipette, Ace and Secret Seven stay in m. Old 'Sidra Natural Trabanco (Pecado del Paraiso)' replaced: the maker's page lists Pecado del Paraíso as a non-alcoholic refreshing drink, so the shelf uses Trabanco's named natural ciders and Pecado Natural. Aspall Blush renamed to Perronelle's Blush per Wikipedia. No version years beyond those on retrieved pages. Sheppy's, Galipette, Hawkstone, Ace have no register entries (no retrieved page). Magners placed under English cider (alias Irish cider) as the only British-Isles cider kind. Pommeau and ice cider are new kinds; Bordelet pommeau and Henney's Frome Valley left out (snippet-only). Asturias and Pays d'Auge Wikipedia pages not found (404)."
